# Victor — the local half of Medusa's chat assistant (2026-09-17).
#
# Victor is Vicky's twin: same chat store, same tools, same reach into the
# image and video generation API. What differs is where the tokens come from —
# Vicky is a `claude -p` subprocess on the operator's Anthropic login, Victor is
# this Ollama model, on this machine, costing nothing per turn.
#
# Deliberately NO `SYSTEM` line. Victor's standing rules are read fresh from
# VICKY_RULES.md on every single turn (medusa_victor.system_prompt()), exactly
# as Vicky's are — baking them in here would freeze them at the moment this
# model was built and an edit to the rules file would silently stop taking
# effect. This Modelfile carries the identity and the runtime dials only.
#
# Rebuild with:  ollama create victor -f config/Victor.Modelfile
FROM qwen3.6:35b-a3b

# A tool loop replays the whole transcript on every turn (Ollama has no
# server-side session to resume, unlike Vicky's --resume), so the context has to
# hold a conversation plus tool results, not just one question.
PARAMETER num_ctx 32768
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
